Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: Fihri OS MacBook Hardware Support Pack — CPU, backlight, GPU, audio, WiFi & HiDPI RDP fixes
 Hardware-detected support package for Apple MacBook / MacBookPro systems running Fihri OS 1.0:
  1. BD PROCHOT CPU throttle fix (canlinux-bdprochot-fix.service clearing MSR 0x1fc
     bit 0 at boot so faulty battery sensors do not pin the CPU at 1.2 GHz).
  2. Display & keyboard backlight permissions (90-canlinux-backlight.rules for
     gmux_backlight and smc::kbd_backlight mode 0664 group video + user group membership).
  3. Dual-GPU stability on Intel+NVIDIA MacBooks (/etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/20-intel-primary.conf
     when Intel i915 is at PCI:0:2:0 alongside NVIDIA, plus kwinrc blurEnabled=false
     and scissorEnabled=true to prevent nouveau GL crashes while keeping rounded corners).
  4. PipeWire audio readiness (human users in audio/video groups, lightdm greeter
     audio masked, pulseaudio masked in favor of PipeWire).
  5. Broadcom BCM4331/BCM43xx STA (wl) module activation when present.
  6. HiDPI-aware FreeRDP shadow geometry recording (/usr/local/bin/freerdp-shadow-start.sh)
     and apport crash-storm guard.
  Includes /usr/local/bin/fihri-hw-detect for Updates UI hardware gating and defensive
  postinst detection: on non-MacBook hardware, MacBook-specific tweaks safely no-op.

